---
// src/components/calculators/content/ConcreteBlockContent.astro
import { blockWallDimensions, getBlockWallMetrics } from '../../../data/block-wall-dimensions';
---

<div class="calc-content-prose">
  <h2>How to Use the Concrete Block (CMU) Calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Whether you are constructing a garden retaining wall, a detached garage wall, or a full perimeter privacy fence, calculating your concrete masonry unit (CMU) requirements accurately prevents mid-job work stoppages and costly mortar reorders:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Enter Wall Dimensions:</strong> Input your wall length and wall height in feet or inches. For stepped walls or changing ground slopes, calculate each level section separately.</li>
    <li><strong>Specify Waste Percentage:</strong> The standard industry allowance is <strong>5% to 10%</strong>. Use 5% for simple straight runs with experienced masons; increase to 10% for walls with multiple 90-degree corners, window/door jambs, or complex cuts.</li>
    <li><strong>Review Mortar & Grout Demands:</strong> Along with total 8×8×16 CMU blocks, check your required bags of Type S mortar mix and cubic yards of core-fill grout. Standard estimates assume standard ⅜-inch bed and head joints.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- Popular Wall Sizes Grid -->
  <h2>Popular Concrete Block Wall Dimensions (Quick Reference Guides)</h2>
  <p>
    Building a wall with standard dimensions? Explore our comprehensive project guides with exact block counts, courses high, units per course, mortar bags, and structural rebar details:
  </p>

  <div class="block-sizes-grid">
    {blockWallDimensions.map((wall) => {
      const m = getBlockWallMetrics(wall.height, wall.length);
      const anchorTitle = `${wall.name} Ft Wall (${m.totalBlocksWithWaste} Blocks)`;
      return (
        <a
          href={`/calculators/concrete-block-calculator/${wall.slug}/`}
          class="block-size-card"
          title={`Concrete block calculator and materials chart for a ${wall.name} ft wall`}
        >
          <div class="block-card-top">
            <span class="block-card-dim">{wall.name} Ft</span>
            <span class="block-card-sqft">{wall.areaSqFt} sq ft</span>
          </div>
          <strong class="block-card-anchor">{anchorTitle}</strong>
          <p class="block-card-desc">{wall.useCase}</p>
          <div class="block-card-footer">
            <span class="block-card-badge">{m.coursesHigh} courses • {m.mortarBags} mortar bags</span>
            <span class="block-card-cta">View Guide →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <h2>Common Concrete Block Wall Dimensions & Materials Reference Table</h2>
  <p>
    Quick reference table showing standard 8×8×16 nominal CMU blocks (+5% waste), courses high, units per course, 80-lb Type S mortar bags, and core fill grout for 10 standard wall sizes:
  </p>

  <div class="table-container">
    <table class="reference-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Wall Size (H×L ft)</th>
          <th>Typical Application</th>
          <th>Area (sq ft)</th>
          <th>Courses High</th>
          <th>8×8×16 Blocks (+5%)</th>
          <th>80-lb Mortar Bags</th>
          <th>Solid Grout (yd³)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {blockWallDimensions.map((wall) => {
          const m = getBlockWallMetrics(wall.height, wall.length);
          return (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <a href={`/calculators/concrete-block-calculator/${wall.slug}/`} class="table-link">
                  <strong>{wall.name} ft</strong>
                </a>
              </td>
              <td>{wall.useCase}</td>
              <td>{wall.areaSqFt} sq ft</td>
              <td>{m.coursesHigh} courses</td>
              <td><strong>{m.totalBlocksWithWaste}</strong></td>
              <td>{m.mortarBags} bags</td>
              <td>{m.groutCuYdsSolid} yd³</td>
            </tr>
          );
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Standard CMU Dimensions and the 1.125 Rule</h2>
  <p>
    In North America, standard concrete masonry units are designated by their nominal dimensions: <strong>8 inches high by 8 inches wide by 16 inches long</strong> (an 8×8×16 block). However, their actual manufactured dimensions are <strong>7⅝" × 7⅝" × 15⅝"</strong>. The remaining ⅜ inch in height and length accounts for the standard mortar joint.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because each block plus mortar joint covers exactly 8" × 16" = 128 square inches (0.8889 sq ft) of wall face:
  </p>
  <div class="formula-callout">
    <code>Number of Blocks = Wall Area (sq ft) × 1.125</code>
  </div>
  <p>
    For example, an 8 ft high by 20 ft long garage wall has an area of 160 sq ft. Multiplying 160 × 1.125 yields exactly 180 net blocks. Adding 5% waste gives 189 blocks to order.
  </p>

  <h2>Mortar Mix Selection: Type S vs. Type N</h2>
  <p>
    Selecting the correct mortar type is essential for structural longevity:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Type S Mortar (Recommended for Most Walls):</strong> Provides high compressive strength (minimum 1,800 psi) and exceptional lateral flexural bond strength. Required by building codes for retaining walls, foundation walls, exterior below-grade walls, and any wall subjected to soil pressure or high wind loads.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Type N Mortar:</strong> Medium strength (minimum 750 psi) with high workability and water retention. Ideal for non-load-bearing interior partitions, above-grade veneer, and decorative garden walls under 4 feet tall in non-seismic zones.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Coverage Rule:</strong> One standard 80-lb pre-mixed bag of Type S or Type N mortar lays approximately <strong>30 to 35 standard 8×8×16 blocks</strong>. For large jobs, masonry cement can be mixed on-site with clean masonry sand at a 1:3 ratio.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<style>
  .block-sizes-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .block-size-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6));
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15));
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .block-size-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  }

  .block-card-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .block-card-dim {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-heading, #ffffff);
  }

  .block-card-sqft {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
  }

  .block-card-anchor {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .block-card-desc {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .block-card-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1));
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .block-card-badge {
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .block-card-cta {
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .table-container {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15));
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .reference-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .reference-table th {
    background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.8);
    color: var(--color-heading, #ffffff);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2));
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .reference-table td {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1));
    color: var(--color-text, #cbd5e1);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .reference-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .table-link {
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .table-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .formula-callout {
    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .formula-callout code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #38bdf8;
  }
</style>
